# Reviewers requested automatically when a pull request touches these paths.
# Paths without an entry get no automatic request; review still happens as
# described in GOVERNANCE.md and CONTRIBUTING.md.
#
# Owners are often the original authors and regular contributors of a path.
# GitHub only requests reviews automatically from owners with write access to the
# repository, i.e., members of the technical and steering committees (see
# GOVERNANCE.md). On pull requests without other assigned reviewers, once they
# are ready for review (not a draft, no `[WIP]` title), the workflow
# .github/workflows/codeowners.yml contacts the other owners once: it requests
# their review if they are members of the GitHub organization and mentions them
# in a single comment otherwise. It does not re-add de-assigned reviewers.
# Initial assignments can be de-assigned, e.g., if for a few select PRs the reviewers
# are not a good choice.
#
# The last matching pattern wins, so keep any broader pattern above the
# narrower ones it should not override.

